      "peer_ticker": "INTC",
      "peer_disclosure_id": "intc_2024_8_D015",
      "relationship": "same_topic",
      "comparison": "Both Intel and NVIDIA disclosed a specific change in the estimated useful lives of their production/operational equipment effective in early 2023, quantifying the financial impact on income statements. NVIDIA increased the useful life of server, storage, and network equipment from three to four or five years, resulting in a $135 million increase in operating income for fiscal 2024. Intel increased the useful life of certain production machinery and equipment from 5 to 8 years, estimating that this change increased gross margin by approximately $2.5 billion and decreased R&D expense by approximately $400 million in 2023. Both cases involve extending asset lives to reduce depreciation expense and boost reported earnings, though the asset types (server/network vs. production machinery) and magnitudes differ significantly.",
