        "nvda_2024_8_P026_S002",
        "nvda_2024_8_P026_S003"
      ],
      "peer_sentence_ids": [
        "intc_2024_8_P028_S001",
        "intc_2024_8_P028_S002"
      ]
    },
    {
      "peer_ticker": "MU",
      "peer_disclosure_id": "mu_2024_8_D017",
      "relationship": "related_topic",
      "comparison": "While NVIDIA reported a specific change in useful life estimates for 2023/2024 affecting $135 million in operating income, Micron (MU) discloses its standard depreciation policies for property, plant, and equipment, including specific useful lives for production equipment (generally 7 years) and other equipment (up to 7 years). Unlike the dynamic change reported by NVIDIA and Intel, Micron's disclosure presents the static range of useful lives used for calculating depreciation expense (straight-line method) without citing a specific recent amendment to those lives in the same fiscal context. Both companies address the estimation of useful lives for production-related assets, but NVIDIA's disclosure is driven by a specific accounting estimate change with quantified earnings impact, whereas Micron's is a standard policy statement.",
      "target_sentence_ids": [
        "nvda_2024_8_P026_S002"
      ],
      "peer_sentence_ids": [
        "mu_2024_8_P027_S001"
      ]
    },
    {
      "peer_ticker": "AMD",
      "peer_disclosure_id": "amd_2024_8_D036",
      "relationship": "related_topic",
      "comparison": "AMD discloses the estimated useful lives for its property and equipment, stating that depreciation is calculated on a straight-line basis over 2 to 15 years for equipment. This contrasts with NVIDIA's disclosure which highlighted a specific change increasing the useful life of server, storage, and network equipment from three to four or five years. AMD's disclosure reflects a static policy range rather than a recent material change in estimates similar to NVIDIA's $135 million income benefit. Additionally, AMD's equipment useful life range (2-15 years) is broader and starts lower than NVIDIA's specific post-change range (4-5 years for most equipment).",
      "target_sentence_ids": [
